    inGuideTitle: 'Inbound Management Guide',
    inGuideIntro: 'This guide explains all inbound-related processes step by step. Easy to follow for new staff.',
    inGuide1Title: '1. What is Inbound Management?',
    inGuide1_1: 'Inbound is the process of registering goods received from vendors into the system.',
    inGuide1_2: 'When you register an inbound, it reflects in stock increase, accounts payable, and income statement purchases.',
    inGuide1_3: 'Whether from a purchase order or direct purchase, stock and purchases are finalized at the inbound registration time.',
    inGuide1_4: 'For Korea imports, select KRW, enter the KRW unit cost and FX rate (KRW per 1 THB); amounts are converted and stored in THB. Enter both KRW and THB amounts to auto-fill the FX rate. KRW and FX remain visible in inbound history.',
    inGuide2Title: '2. Overall Flow',
    inGuide2_1: 'Create PO → Approve → Register Inbound → Stock & Payable updated',
    inGuide2_2: 'Or Direct Purchase → Register Inbound → Same reflection',
    inGuide2_3: 'Bank withdrawal → Link to Inbound to track which inbound was paid',
    inGuide3Title: '3. How to Register New Inbound',
    inGuide3_1: 'Date: Select the actual receipt date.',
    inGuide3_2: 'Vendor: Select the vendor. Add new vendors in Vendor Management first.',
    inGuide3_3: 'Add items: Use 🔍 to search and select items, enter quantity, then click "Add to List".',
    inGuide3_4: 'Edit cost: Items have default cost; you can edit the table if actual cost differs.',
    inGuide3_5: 'Save: Click "Process Inbound" to save. Stock and payable are updated automatically.',
    inGuide4Title: '4. Inbound from Purchase Order',
    inGuide4_1: 'Approved purchase orders have an "Register Inbound" button.',
