    accCompSchedGuideTitle: 'Thailand accounting & tax filing schedule (summary)',
    accCompSchedGuideDisclaimer:
      'Reference only. Actual duties and deadlines vary with law changes, RD/DBD notices, fiscal year-end, industry, and entity type — confirm with a qualified accountant/tax agent.',
    accCompSched_sec1_title: '1. VAT — PP.30 (ภ.พ.30)',
    accCompSched_sec1_body:
      'Most frequent filing\n\n✔ File & pay: due the 15th of the following month in principle (e-filing often allows a short extension)\n\nExample: March tax period → around 15 April (or ~23 April if extended)',
    accCompSched_sec2_title: '2. Withholding tax — PND forms (ภ.ง.ด.)',
    accCompSched_sec2_body:
      'When WHT applies on salaries, contractors, services, etc.\n\n✔ File & pay: due the 7th of the following month in principle (e-filing often allows extension)\n\nExample: March payments → around 7 April (or ~15 April if extended)',
    accCompSched_sec3_title: '3. PND 51 — mid-year corporate income tax',
    accCompSched_sec3_body:
      'Half-year prepayment / filing\n\n✔ File: within 2 months after 6 months from the start of the accounting period (timing varies by fiscal year)\n\nExample: Jan–Dec fiscal year → often around end of June',
    accCompSched_sec4_title: '4. PND 50 — year-end corporate income tax',
    accCompSched_sec4_body:
      'Final CIT after financials are closed\n\n✔ File & pay: within 150 days after the fiscal year-end\n\nExample: 31 Dec year-end → around end of May next year',
    accCompSched_sec5_title: '5. Annual financial statements — DBD filing',
    accCompSched_sec5_body:
      'File audited/stated financials with the Department of Business Development\n\n✔ Due: within 5 months after fiscal year-end\n\nExample: 31 Dec year-end → around end of May next year (may overlap PND 50 timing)',
    accCompSched_sec6_title: '6. Annual general meeting (AGM)',
    accCompSched_sec6_body:
      'Mandatory ordinary shareholders’ meeting\n\n✔ Hold: within 4 months after fiscal year-end\n\nExample: 31 Dec year-end → around end of April next year',
